<section class="section about-tint"><div class="section-shell"><div class="section-heading"><h2>What's in Australian tap water?</h2></div><p>Australian mains water is treated to meet the Australian Drinking Water Guidelines, so it's safe to drink. But treatment and old pipes still leave things behind that affect taste, skin and appliances.</p><div class="filter-facts filter-facts--v2"><article class="fact-card"><div class="fx fx--cl" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fx-water"></span><span class="fx-bub fx-bub--1">Cl</span><span class="fx-bub fx-bub--2">Cl</span><span class="fx-bub fx-bub--3">Cl</span><span class="fx-bub fx-bub--4">Cl</span><span class="fx-bub fx-bub--5">Cl</span><span class="fx-shine"></span></div><span class="filter-detail-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 3h6m-5 0v6l-6 9a2 2 0 0 0 2 3h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-3l-6-9V3M7 15h10"/></svg></span><h3>Chlorine and chloramines</h3><p>added by water authorities to disinfect the supply. They cause the &quot;pool&quot; taste and smell and can dry out skin and hair.</p></article><article class="fact-card"><div class="fx fx--sed" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fx-water fx-water--murky"></span><span class="fx-grain fx-grain--1"></span><span class="fx-grain fx-grain--2"></span><span class="fx-grain fx-grain--3"></span><span class="fx-grain fx-grain--4"></span><span class="fx-grain fx-grain--5"></span><span class="fx-grain fx-grain--6"></span><span class="fx-grain fx-grain--7"></span><span class="fx-grain fx-grain--8"></span><span class="fx-bed"></span></div><span class="filter-detail-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 5h18l-7 8v7l-4 2v-9L3 5Z"/><path d="M8 8h.01M12 8h.01M16 8h.01"/></svg></span><h3>Sediment, rust and silt</h3><p>picked up from ageing mains and household pipes. They cloud water and wear out tapware and appliances.</p></article><article class="fact-card"><div class="fx fx--metal" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fx-pipe"><span class="fx-pipe__joint"></span></span><span class="fx-drip fx-drip--1"></span><span class="fx-drip fx-drip--2"></span><span class="fx-drip fx-drip--3"></span><span class="fx-pool"></span></div><span class="filter-detail-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 3 9 5-9 5-9-5 9-5Zm-9 9 9 5 9-5M3 16l9 5 9-5"/></svg></span><h3>Heavy metals</h3><p>such as lead and copper, which can leach from old plumbing fittings.</p></article><article class="fact-card"><div class="fx fx--org" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fx-mol fx-mol--a"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 56" width="64" height="56"><line x1="32" y1="7" x2="7" y2="49" stroke="#a9c4d3" stroke-width="2.5"></line><line x1="32" y1="7" x2="57" y2="49" stroke="#a9c4d3" stroke-width="2.5"></line><line x1="7" y1="49" x2="57" y2="49" stroke="#a9c4d3" stroke-width="2.5"></line><circle cx="32" cy="7" r="7" fill="#5d9e3f"></circle><circle cx="7" cy="49" r="7" fill="#267aa9"></circle><circle cx="57" cy="49" r="7" fill="#d9822b"></circle></svg></span><span class="fx-mol fx-mol--b"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 56" width="64" height="56"><line x1="32" y1="7" x2="7" y2="49" stroke="#a9c4d3" stroke-width="2.5"></line><line x1="32" y1="7" x2="57" y2="49" stroke="#a9c4d3" stroke-width="2.5"></line><line x1="7" y1="49" x2="57" y2="49" stroke="#a9c4d3" stroke-width="2.5"></line><circle cx="32" cy="7" r="7" fill="#5d9e3f"></circle><circle cx="7" cy="49" r="7" fill="#267aa9"></circle><circle cx="57" cy="49" r="7" fill="#d9822b"></circle></svg></span><span class="fx-mol fx-mol--c"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 56" width="64" height="56"><line x1="32" y1="7" x2="7" y2="49" stroke="#a9c4d3" stroke-width="2.5"></line><line x1="32" y1="7" x2="57" y2="49" stroke="#a9c4d3" stroke-width="2.5"></line><line x1="7" y1="49" x2="57" y2="49" stroke="#a9c4d3" stroke-width="2.5"></line><circle cx="32" cy="7" r="7" fill="#5d9e3f"></circle><circle cx="7" cy="49" r="7" fill="#267aa9"></circle><circle cx="57" cy="49" r="7" fill="#d9822b"></circle></svg></span></div><span class="filter-detail-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="6" cy="7" r="3"/><circle cx="18" cy="8" r="3"/><circle cx="12" cy="18" r="3"/><path d="m9 7 6 1M7 10l3 5m6-4-3 4"/></svg></span><h3>Organic chemicals</h3><p>traces of pesticides, herbicides and volatile organic compounds (VOCs).</p></article><article class="fact-card"><div class="fx fx--hard" aria-hidden="true"><span class="fx-tap"></span><span class="fx-stream"></span><span class="fx-surface"><i class="fx-scale fx-scale--1"></i><i class="fx-scale fx-scale--2"></i><i class="fx-scale fx-scale--3"></i><i class="fx-scale fx-scale--4"></i><i class="fx-scale fx-scale--5"></i><i class="fx-scale fx-scale--6"></i><i class="fx-scale fx-scale--7"></i></span></div><span class="filter-detail-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2S5 10 5 15a7 7 0 0 0 14 0c0-5-7-13-7-13Z"/><path d="m9 14 3-2 3 2-1 4h-4Z"/></svg></span><h3>Hardness</h3><p>calcium and magnesium that leave limescale. Melbourne water is soft, while supplies in places like Adelaide and Perth are much harder.</p></article></div><div class="u-s4"><a class="text-link" href="<?php echo $baseUrl; ?>/benefits.php">Explore filtration benefits &#8594;</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-shell"><div class="section-heading section-heading--center"><h2>The three filtration stages</h2></div><div class="filter-stage-table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Filtration stages comparison" tabindex="0"><table class="filter-stage-table"><caption class="filter-sr-only">The three filtration stages: cartridges, functions and benefits</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Cartridge</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">Why it matters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><span class="filter-stage-badge">01</span></th><td class="filter-stage-cartridge">10 μm antibacterial pleated PP sediment filter</td><td>Traps sand, silt, rust and micro-particles. Antibacterial media reduces microbial growth on the filter itself.</td><td>Protects stages 2 and 3, extends their life and keeps grit out of your plumbing.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span class="filter-stage-badge">02</span></th><td class="filter-stage-cartridge">1 μm scale-reducing carbon (CTO) filter</td><td>Reduces chlorine, chloramines, VOCs, pesticides, herbicides, iron, hydrogen sulfide and some heavy metals. Helps limit scale.</td><td>Protects tapware, showers, baths and appliances from staining, scale and odour.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><span class="filter-stage-badge">03</span></th><td class="filter-stage-cartridge">1 μm coconut shell carbon (CTO) filter</td><td>Polishes taste and odour and removes remaining chemicals and fine particles.</td><td>Cleaner-tasting water for drinking, cooking and making tea and coffee.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section class="section filter-limits" aria-labelledby="filter-limits-title"><div class="section-shell filter-limits-layout"><div class="filter-limits-photo"><img src="<?php echo $baseUrl; ?>/assets/images/what-this-system-img.webp" alt="Family drinking water together at home" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="filter-limits-content"><div class="section-heading filter-limits-heading"><h2 id="filter-limits-title">What this system won't do</h2><p>Being clear about the limits helps you choose the right setup.</p></div><ul class="filter-limit-grid"><li class="filter-limit-card"><span class="filter-limit-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2S5 10 5 15a7 7 0 0 0 14 0c0-5-7-13-7-13Z"/><path d="M9 15h6"/></svg></span><p>It isn't a disinfection unit. It's designed for treated mains water, not untreated tank, bore or creek water. Those need testing and extra treatment such as UV.</p></li><li class="filter-limit-card"><span class="filter-limit-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M15 7h-6v10m0-6h5"/></svg></span><p>It doesn't remove fluoride. The carbon stages aren't designed for it.</p></li><li class="filter-limit-card"><span class="filter-limit-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 3 8 5v8l-8 5-8-5V8Z"/><path d="m4 8 8 5 8-5m-8 5v8"/></svg></span><p>It isn't a salt-based softener. Stage 2 helps limit scale, but very hard water may still need a dedicated softener.</p></li><li class="filter-limit-card"><span class="filter-limit-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 3 8 3v6c0 5-8 9-8 9s-8-4-8-9V6Z"/><path d="m9 10 6 6m0-6-6 6"/></svg></span><p>The standard cartridges aren't PFAS-rated.</p></li></ul><div class="filter-limits-link"><a class="text-link" href="<?php echo $baseUrl; ?>/#pfas-title">Read about PFAS in Australian water &#8594;</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-shell about-story"><div><h2>Why three stages instead of one?</h2><p>A single cartridge trying to catch everything clogs quickly, because sand and rust block the fine carbon before it can do its job. Splitting the work into three stages fixes that. The coarse sediment filter takes the grit, which leaves the two 1 micron carbon stages free to deal with chlorine, chemicals and taste.</p>
<p>The result is steadier flow, longer cartridge life and better filtration than one cartridge doing it all. It's also why the larger 20&quot; x 4.5&quot; Big Blue size matters. More filter media means more water filtered before a change is due.</p></div><div class="story-media">
  <img class="img-placeholder" src="<?php echo $baseUrl; ?>/assets/images/why-three-stages-img.webp" alt="Why three stages instead of one">
</div></div></section>
<section class="section suits-band-section"><div class="section-shell"><div class="suits-band"><div class="suits-band__head"><h2>Where it suits</h2></div><div class="suits-band__body"><p>The system suits houses of any size, new builds and renovations. It also fits small commercial sites like offices, cafes and restaurants that want filtered water across the premises. Your plumber installs it on the main supply line, so it covers the kitchen, bathrooms, laundry and garden taps in one go.</p><a class="button" href="<?php echo $baseUrl; ?>/request-a-quote.php">Book a Free In-Home Assessment</a></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section about-tint"><div class="section-shell filter-care-grid"><div class="filter-care-card"><span class="filter-detail-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 5a6 6 0 0 0-7 7l-4 4a3 3 0 0 0 4 4l4-4a6 6 0 0 0 8-7l-4 4-4-4 4-4Z"/></svg></span><h2>Installation requirements</h2><ul class="filter-checks"><li>Installed on the cold water line, downstream of any backflow prevention device</li><li>Must be installed by a licensed plumber to AS/NZS 3500</li><li>Shut-off valves fitted either side so cartridges can be changed without turning off the whole house</li><li>The system is flushed thoroughly before first use</li></ul><p class="u-s5">The system needs wall space of roughly 575 mm wide by 760 mm high, usually on an external wall near the water meter.</p></div><div class="filter-care-card filter-care-card--blue"><span class="filter-detail-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="16" rx="2"/><path d="M7 3v4m10-4v4M3 10h18m-13 5 3 3 5-5"/></svg></span><h2>Maintenance</h2><p>Plan on replacing cartridges every 6 to 12 months. Homes with more sediment or bigger households sit at the shorter end. Each change uses the spanner supplied with the system and takes about 5 to 10 minutes per cartridge. When you change them, check the O-rings and seals and replace any that look worn.</p>
<p>We'll remind you when a change is due.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section upg-section"><div class="section-shell upg-layout"><div class="filter-upgrade-card"><span class="filter-detail-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v18M3 12h18"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><h2>Optional upgrades</h2><ul class="filter-checks"><li><strong>Pre-filter</strong> for high-sediment supplies, which extends the life of the main cartridges</li><li><strong>Smart flow meter</strong> to track how much water has passed through each filter</li><li><strong>Multi-level installation kits</strong> for tighter spaces</li></ul></div><div class="upg-media">
  <img class="img-placeholder" src="<?php echo $baseUrl; ?>/assets/images/optional-upgrades-img.webp" alt="Optional upgrades">
</div></div></section>
<section class="section cert-section"><div class="section-shell"><div class="filter-certification-card cert-full"><h2>Certification and testing</h2><p>The system is WaterMark certified, which means it meets Australian requirements for plumbing products. It has also been tested to AS/NZS 4020:2018 and passed every category: taste, appearance, microbial growth, cytotoxicity, mutagenicity, metals and organic compounds. Housings are food-grade, with stainless steel mounting brackets.</p><a class="text-link" href="<?php echo $baseUrl; ?>/about-us.php#about-standards-title">Learn about our standards &#8594;</a><p>For installer training and support, <a class="text-link" href="<?php echo $baseUrl; ?>/become-a-dealer.php">become a PureLine dealer</a>.</p><p></p></div></div></section>    <section class="section section--faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
        <div class="section-shell faq-layout">
            <div class="faq-heading reveal"><h2 id="faq-title">Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
            <div class="faq-list reveal reveal--late">
                <article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-1"><span>Q. What is a Big Blue filter?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-1" hidden><p>&quot;Big Blue&quot; is the common name for a 20&quot; x 4.5&quot; filter housing. The larger size lets more water through with less pressure drop and holds more filter media, so cartridges last longer than standard 10&quot; filters.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-2"><span>Q. What does &quot;1 micron&quot; mean?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-2" hidden><p>It's the size of particle the cartridge is rated to trap. One micron is a thousandth of a millimetre, far smaller than anything you can see.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-3"><span>Q. What does a whole house water filter remove from Australian tap water?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-3" hidden><p>This system reduces chlorine by more than 95%, VOCs and pesticides by more than 90%, and also reduces chloramines, sediment, rust, iron and some heavy metals.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-4"><span>Q. Is 30 litres per minute enough for my house?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-4" hidden><p>For most homes, yes. That flow covers a shower, a tap and a washing machine running at the same time in a typical household.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-5"><span>Q. How long do the cartridges last?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-5" hidden><p>Between 6 and 12 months. The exact life depends on how much water you use and how much sediment is in your supply.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-6" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-6"><span>Q. Can I change the cartridges myself?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-6" hidden><p>Yes. The system comes with a spanner, and each cartridge takes about 5 to 10 minutes. We can also do it for you.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-7"><span>Q. Does it work with a rainwater tank?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-7" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-7" hidden><p>It can, with a suitable pre-filter, but it isn't a disinfection system. Untreated water should be tested first and may need UV treatment as well.</p></div>
</article>
<article class="faq-item">
<h3 class="faq-item__heading"><button class="faq-trigger" type="button" id="faq-question-8" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-answer-8"><span>Q. Is the system suitable for commercial premises?</span><span class="faq-trigger__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3>
<div class="faq-answer" id="faq-answer-8" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-question-8" hidden><p>Yes. It's designed for high-flow, whole-premises use, including offices and restaurants. We'll check your demand at the assessment.</p></div>
</article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

